                             Requirements
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


 LogicBBS requires kickstart version 2.x or higher. A minimum space of
 1 megabyte free on your HOST drive. and furthermore you will need
 a fully installed workbench, and the reqtools.library.
 LogicBBS can be started from a diskdrive or harddrive. A harddrive
 installation is what is expected as the filebase will not be able to run
 without enough free space on HOST drive.
 Memory requirements is minimum, you can start off with 2 megs of free memory.
 It all depends on your configuration of LogicBBS.

 example:
   1 Node with 16/16K r/w hydra cachebuffers and 16K serialcache and
   10K internal diskcache takes only 435K memory.
   An additional node requires 125K extra memory. with the same settings as
   with the 1 node system.


 Lookup list
 -----------

 - Kickstart 2.x or higher (Software version or hardware(ROM) version)
 - reqtools.library
 - 1 megabyte free diskdrive space (after installation of LogicBBS)
 - Stack for LogicBBS/Server should be set to 16384 bytes.
   (Change it through ICON->INFORMATION menu in workbench, if not already set)

 If you want the bbs to autostart at reset, put the mainprogram file, and its
 icon into the WBSTARTUP drawer, and make sure you load workbench at startup.



 To start Rexx doors, you need the command "RX" in your C: directory,
 the system will NOT search in patched directories, used with the "PATH ADD"
 command. So you must copy the RX program yourself from the REXXC directory
 into your C: path.

